; Fixture for tools/lenfix/scan.py --selftest. NOT part of any package; it is
; read only by the self-test, which walks this directory instead of packages/.
;
; ★★★IT EXISTS BECAUSE THE FIRST SELF-TEST DIED OF ITS OWN HARVEST. It asserted
; that `get_identifier_token(buf)` comes out CHAIN-ADJACENT — the real chain the
; tool was calibrated on — and the moment that chain was converted the assertion
; failed, reporting "the fixpoint does not fire" about a fixpoint that works.
; A self-test keyed on a CANDIDATE is a self-test with an expiry date; this one
; is keyed on a shape the tree cannot take away.

; leaf: walks its buffer, but its own signature carries no length (the length
; belongs to the OTHER parameter). refslice calls this LENLESS.
function leaf_walks_no_len(buf: pointer[char], word: Slice[char]) returns bool
{
    var i: int 0
    while i < word.length
    {
        if (*(buf + i) as int) <> (word[i] as int)
            return false
        set i: i + 1
    }
    true
}

; forwarder: carries (buf, len) in its signature — perfect ADJACENT form — and
; proves NOTHING itself; only the callee proves buf is a buffer. This is the
; class refslice discards as UNWALKED, and the one this tool exists to find.
function forwarder_pairs_and_forwards(buf: pointer[char], len: int) returns bool
{
    if len < 2
        return false
    leaf_walks_no_len(buf, Slice[char](2, "as"))
}

; negative control: same ADJACENT shape, forwards to a callee that proves
; nothing about the buffer. Must NOT come out as a chain candidate — otherwise
; the fixpoint is propagating on the call alone rather than on the proof.
function sink_proves_nothing(p: pointer[char], q: int) returns bool
    q > 0

function forwarder_to_nothing(buf: pointer[char], len: int) returns bool
    sink_proves_nothing(buf, len)
